{"action": "final", "output": {
  "research_concepts": [
    "shaper (low-usage, high structural influence) role travel",
    "cut-heavy vs drive-heavy offensive play-type profiles",
    "role portability after team change"
  ],
  "methodological_questions": [
    "How to reliably classify shapers as cut-heavy or drive-heavy given known play-type labeling artifacts?",
    "How to measure portability of a shaper's structural influence across teams?",
    "Is the sample of shaper movers large enough to detect a difference in portability between cut-heavy and drive-heavy profiles?",
    "How to separate the effect of play-type profile from confounding factors like team system fit and menu similarity?"
  ],
  "historical_evidence": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-057",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Cut- vs drive-based connector portability: Pre-move cut share positively predicts portability (rho=+0.265 p=0.011), drive share negatively (rho=-0.278 p=0.007). Top cut tercile 65% portable, median Delta +0.167; bottom 35% median -0.039. LOO AUC 0.622; permutation p=0.005. Sample 92 connector movers."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025",
      "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
      "finding": "Play-type labeling audit: OTHER ends in fouls 36%, inflating PPP; DRIVE shows 12pp below foul benchmark (foul leakage). Only 0.7% of possessions map to a real play type via initiation_type. Suggests DRIVE and CUT labels may be contaminated."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-096",
      "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
      "finding": "Play-type classifier assisted-flag leak: SPOT_UP 2.83 PPP (100% makes) because assisted flag exists only on makes; after rewrite SPOT_UP ~1.16, TRANSITION ~1.20. Indicates play-type classification errors may affect possession-level labels for multiple play types including CUT and DRIVE."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-029",
      "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
      "finding": "DRIVE lifts are flat and non-decaying across lags; within-team DRIVE lag-1 effect collapses to near zero. Team-quality confound identified. Callable play-type horizons = 0. DRIVE signal is not a reliable stable property."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-087",
      "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
      "finding": "Connector-mover pairing variants: organizer-connector gap CI includes 0 after correcting menu-similarity confound. KW p=0.047 is population-level, pairwise is suggestive. Sample 92 movers, small, confounded by menu similarity."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-016",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Portability feasibility gate passed: 296 movers, decoy fraction 1.00, vacuity rho=0.007. Indicates the mover/decoy design works, but requires sufficient movers (>=25) and decoys."
    }
  ],
  "failed_approaches": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025",
      "what_failed": "Direct use of raw play-type labels for DRIVE and OTHER",
      "why": "Foul leakage inflates OTHER PPP and depresses DRIVE PPP; initiation_type mapping covers only 0.7% of possessions."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-096",
      "what_failed": "Possession-level play-type inference before rewriting inferrer",
      "why": "Assisted flag only present on made baskets created 100% make rate for SPOT_UP and biased other play-type PPPs, potentially affecting CUT/DRIVE classification."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-087",
      "what_failed": "Simple connector-mover pairing rules without correcting for menu similarity",
      "why": "Apparent organizer-connector gap disappeared after correcting for menu-similarity confound; small sample and confounding limit reliability."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-028",
      "what_failed": "action_sequences as a stable tactical signal",
      "why": "Stability CV=0.919, only 23 games/46 team-observations, average sample per key 6.9; measurement too unstable."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_establishes": [
    "Among 92 connector movers, pre-move cut share positively correlates with portability (Delta) and drive share negatively correlates.",
    "Cut-heavy connectors have a median portability Delta ~0.167 vs -0.039 for bottom tercile, with a LOO AUC of 0.622.",
    "Play-type labels for DRIVE and CUT are subject to known artifacts (foul leakage, assisted-flag bias) that could affect classification of cut-heavy vs drive-heavy.",
    "DRIVE signals show flat, non-decaying lifts and team-quality confounding, making them less reliable as a stable individual property.",
    "Mover/decoy portability designs require at least 25 movers and adequate decoys to be feasible; connector portability results are sensitive to menu-similarity confounding."
  ],
  "evidence_does_not_establish": [
    "Whether the cut vs drive portability difference holds specifically for shapers (low-usage, positive residual structural influence) as opposed to the broader connector label.",
    "Whether the effect can be detected with only n=24 shaper movers.",
    "Whether the relationship survives correction for the play-type labeling artifacts identified in FAM:SF-CHT-025 and FAM:SF-PAP-096.",
    "The causal mechanism: whether cut-heavy roles are inherently more portable or artifact of offensive system stability."
  ],
  "own_inferences": [
    "The term 'shapers' limits the population to low-usage, high-influence players, which likely reduces the available mover pool to n=24 (as recorded).",
    "With n=24, even a true correlation similar to the one found for connectors (rho~0.27) would be underpowered (power < 30%), making a hypothesis test unlikely to yield a conclusive result.",
    "Any classification of players into cut-heavy vs drive-heavy using the current play-type labels must first validate that label artifacts do not systematically bias one group.",
    "The presence of menu-similarity confounding and team system effects (FAM:SF-CHT-087, FAM:SF-CHT-029) suggests that portability differences may not solely reflect the player's inherent style but also the fit with the new team's structure."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Exact overlap between the connector definition used in FAM:SF-CHT-057 and the shaper definition in the current question.",
    "Whether the play-type label fixes (post PAP-096 and CHT-025) have been applied to the data available on 2026-08-08.",
    "The number of shaper movers with sufficient possessions in both CUT and DRIVE to classify them reliably; many shapers have low usage, creating sparsity.",
    "Whether decoy players can be matched reliably for shapers given their low usage and specialized roles."
  ],
  "historical_effect": {
    "changed_decision": "yes",
    "explanation": "Without historical evidence, the question might appear testable as a straightforward extension of portability work. The retrieved records show: (1) the hypothesis is partly supported for connectors, giving a prior; (2) play-type labels for DRIVE/CUT have known artifacts that could bias classification; (3) DRIVE-based measures show team-quality confounding and flat memory; (4) small samples (n=92 for connectors) already limit confidence, and the shaper subset of n=24 is far smaller. This shifts the assessment from 'proceed cautiously' to 'do not proceed' because the sample is insufficient and measurement validity is in doubt."
  },
  "testability": {
    "p_testable": 0.15,
    "blocking_constraints": [
      {
        "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
        "text": "Only n=24 shaper movers are available; power to detect a correlation of 0.27 at alpha=0.05 is below 30%, and the MDE is likely too large to be useful."
      },
      {
        "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
        "text": "Play-type labels for DRIVE and CUT have documented artifacts (foul leakage, assisted-flag bias) that may misclassify possessions; without validated fixed labels, the cut-heavy vs drive-heavy distinction is unreliable."
      },
      {
        "code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
        "text": "Shapers are low-usage players; many may have too few CUT or DRIVE possessions to produce stable within-player play-type shares, leading to noisy classification."
      },
      {
        "code": "CONFOUNDING",
        "text": "Team system and menu-similarity confounds documented in connector portability studies could bias the portability difference between cut-heavy and drive-heavy groups."
      }
    ]
  },
  "prior_work": {
    "already_answered": "partly",
    "cited": [
      "FAM:SF-CHT-057",
      "FAM:SF-CHT-025",
      "FAM:SF-PAP-096",
      "FAM:SF-CHT-029",
      "FAM:SF-CHT-087"
    ],
    "summary": "FAM:SF-CHT-057 directly tested cut vs drive portability among connectors and found a positive signal (cut-heavy more portable). However, it did not focus on shapers specifically, and the effect has not been replicated with validated play-type labels after known artifacts were fixed. The current question narrows the population to shapers and demands a test with only 24 units, which is unaddressed by prior work."
  },
  "risks": [
    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
      "text": "n=24 shaper movers yields very low power; a true effect comparable to the connector finding (rho~0.27) would be undetectable with conventional power."
    },
    {
      "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
      "text": "Play-type classification for DRIVE vs CUT is affected by known artifacts (foul leakage, assisted-flag leak); reliability of the cut-heavy vs drive-heavy grouping is not established with the available data version."
    },
    {
      "code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
      "text": "Low-usage shapers may have few CUT or DRIVE initiations, making play-type share estimates unstable and group assignment noisy."
    },
    {
      "code": "CONFOUNDING",
      "text": "Portability may be influenced by team offensive style, role fit, and menu similarity, not purely by the player's play-type profile; without controls, the comparison is confounded."
    },
    {
      "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
      "text": "Players who move teams are a non-random subset; shapers who change teams may be systematically different from non-movers, affecting generalizability."
    },
    {
      "code": "BASE_RATE",
      "text": "The base rate of cut-heavy shapers among the limited mover pool may be too low for a meaningful tercile split or continuous analysis."
    },
    {
      "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
      "text": "If the analysis involves multiple definitions of portability or play-type thresholds, multiplicity adjustments will further erode power."
    },
    {
      "code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD",
      "text": "Using post-move data to define shaper status or cut-heaviness could leak information; pre-move data only must be used."
    }
  ],
  "predicted_outcome": {
    "supported": 0.1,
    "rejected": 0.05,
    "untestable": 0.5,
    "artifact": 0.2,
    "uncertain": 0.15
  },
  "decision": "do_not_proceed",
  "design": {
    "estimand": "Difference in portability (Delta, one minus cosine similarity of teammate play-type mix pre- vs post-move) between cut-heavy shapers and drive-heavy shapers, where a shaper is defined as a player with below-median usage and positive residual structural influence (L_res) in the pre-move season, and cut-heavy is defined as a pre-move CUT share exceeding a minimum threshold (e.g., top tercile among shapers) relative to DRIVE share.",
    "unit": "Player-mover (a shaper who changed teams between consecutive NBA seasons).",
    "sample": "All identified shaper movers from 2022-23 to 2025-26 with at least 10 initiations in both CUT and DRIVE play types in the pre-move season, and with at least 3 decoy matches available. Minimum viable sample for 80% power to detect rho=0.27 is approximately 85 movers; current available n=24 is insufficient.",
    "power": "Proposed design requires at least 85 shaper movers; with n=24, power is estimated below 30% for a correlation effect size of 0.27 (alpha=0.05, two-sided). A feasibility simulation should be run to compute MDE given the actual sample size.",
    "controls": "Pre-move team offensive system (play-type mix), player usage, position, age, and a menu-similarity index between pre- and post-move teams to control for system fit. Use decoy-based placebo displacement difference to remove baseline confounds.",
    "falsification": "Permutation test: shuffle cut/drive labels among shaper movers 5,000 times to build null distribution of portability differences. Pre-register that the observed difference must exceed the 95th percentile. Also, test that the effect is not driven by a single team or season with leave-one-out and year-split robustness checks.",
    "multiplicity": "Single primary hypothesis: cut-heavy shapers have higher portability (Delta) than drive-heavy shapers. Secondary analyses split by terciles with adjusted alpha. No fishing across multiple play-type definitions.",
    "decision_rule": "Two-sided Spearman correlation between continuous pre-move CUT-DRIVE share difference and portability Delta, with alpha=0.05. Supported if p<0.05 and the effect survives all pre-registered robustness checks. Rejected if p>0.05 with a pre-specified equivalence bound (MDE) indicating adequate power. Untestable if post-hoc power analysis shows power <80% for the observed effect size.",
    "data_version": "Play-by-play and derived initiation records from NBA 2022-23 through 2025-26 seasons, with play-type labels generated by the post-fix inferrer (correcting flagged artifacts from FAM:SF-PAP-096 and FAM:SF-CHT-025). Garbage time excluded. Only regular-season games used for pre-move and post-move measurement windows."
  }
}}

